Z||000009||Jake2m4||05-12-2001||07:24 PM||||My fiero started smoking twice, but not truely flaming and no damage.<P>The first time I had left the engine vents off for a couple of weeks while it sat and I worked on it.  Lots of pinestraw fell down onto the exhaust sys. and started to burn, luckily it was still in the driveway, and I got the pinestraw out.  That was a stupid mistake that won't be repeated.<P>The second time it appears that the anti freeze leaked from coolant hose and smoked or evaporated.  I haven't fixed it yet, but I have a clutch to fix first.<P>Hey a 300 dollar car is bound to have its problems.  Plus it was from a police auction so I can assume it wasn't well maintained.<P><BR>------------------<BR>'85 Fiero Sport Coupe<BR>'95 Pontiac Grand AM SE<p>[This message has been edited by Jake2m4 (edited 05-12-2001).]||||reg||1
